When demonstrations show color 2 appearing in some horizontal and vertical gaps between same-color markers, that establishes only a possible geometric operation, not the criterion selecting which lines are transformed. Do not blanket-fill all aligned intervals in the test: several broad interval/ray submissions were rejected in this recurrence despite demos containing some filled gaps. Later demos show selected horizontal/vertical line gaps, but the selection rule remains unresolved unless all changed and unchanged examples can be explained together.

